### Auth Service Verification Tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@userServiceUrl = http://localhost:3002

### 1. Register User (Happy Path)
# This calls Auth Service, which calls User Service
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "testuser@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "fullName": "Test User",
    "phone": "0912345678",
    "role": "PASSENGER"
}

### 2. Login User (Happy Path)
# Should return accessToken and refreshToken
# Response also includes User Profile from User Service
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "testuser@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Get Current User (Me)
# Use accessToken from login response
@authToken = <REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN>
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4. Refresh Token
# Use refreshToken from login response
@refreshToken = <REPLACE_WITH_REFRESH_TOKEN>
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshToken}}

### 5. Logout
# Use the NEW refreshToken from refresh response (due to rotation)
@newRefreshToken = <REPLACE_WITH_NEW_REFRESH_TOKEN>
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{newRefreshToken}}

### 6. Verify Logout (Try to refresh again)
# Should fail (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{newRefreshToken}}

### 7. Helper: Delete User from User Service (Cleanup)
# If you have admin access or direct DB access via User Service
DELETE {{userServiceUrl}}/users/<USER_ID>
